Example Questions
		• What outcome is this engagement going to create for our client?
		• What are the options to get our client to that outcome?
		• What can I personally do to maximize the probability of the outcome?
		• Do I understand how my client wants to solve the problem?
		• How can I add value beyond the contract?
		• What matters most to my client, and how can I stay ahead of their information needs?
		• Create a value add outside of the SOW – “SOW to Customer Love"
		• What is the client culture and how can the team adjust their approach to match the client working style and standards?
		• What are the personalities on the client and Slalom team and how can individuals be motivated to produce their best work?
		• Have expectations been clearly set across the client and Slalom team and are changes to plan clearly communicated?
		• Get to know the extended client team to build relationships beyond your engagement  and identify potential opportunities for Slalom.
		• No engagement executes according to the original plan – be prepared for change and implement structures that help the team respond to the change.
		• Be prepared to adjust as you learn more about the engagement objectives, risks and client culture.
		• Don’t be afraid to try a different approach if something is not working.
		• Be a role model for the team on how to respond to challenges and changes. Help to instill confidence in the team that they can successfully navigate the challenges ahead.
